{"abstract":[{"text":"The records of the events a tracker tracks, in the order tracked: what a delivery reads.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence ends once the tracker’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/finish()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called, or its every copy is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, for the next read, so none tracked before a delivery starts, or between two, is lost."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A read whose task is cancelled returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and takes nothing: the next read gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record it was waiting for, and every one after. A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/noOp","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tracker’s records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One task reads at a time. The first iterator to read holds the records until its iteration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends or the iterator is released, as it is when its task ends. An iterator that reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"meanwhile waits its turn, logging a warning as it starts to, then reads on from the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record; several wait in the order they came, and one whose task is cancelled while it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waits returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So a delivery started right after a cancelled one has stopped, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while it is stopping, delivers every record the cancelled one didn’t read.","type":"text"}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/Sci"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Tracker.Records","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Records"}],"externalID":"s:8Trackers7TrackerV7RecordsV","roleHeading":"Structure","extendedModule":"Trackers","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Records.swift#L27","fileName":"Records.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/tracker\/records-swift.struct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncIterator"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\